  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "num": "01",
      "en": "Ralph Emerson once said that the purpose of life is not to be happy, but to be useful, to be {loving} , to make some difference in the world.While {we} appreciate such words of {wisdom} , we {rarely} try to follow them in our lives.",
      "cn": "拉尔夫·爱默生曾经说过，生活的目的不是为了快乐，而是为了成为有用的人， <u> 富有爱心 </u> ，并在这个世界上留下一些影响。虽然 <u> 我们 </u> 欣赏这样的 <u> 智慧 </u> 之言，却 <u> 很少 </u> 在生活中去践行它们。"
    },
    {
      "num": "02",
      "en": "Most people prefer to live a good life {themselves} , ignoring their responsibilities to the world.This narrow {perception} of a good life may provide {short-term} benefits, but is sure to lead to {long-term} {harm} and {suffering} .A good life {based} on comfort and {luxury} may eventually lead to more {pain} because we {spoil} our {health} and even our character, {principles} , {ideals} , and relationships.",
      "cn": "大多数人更喜欢 <u> 自己 </u> 过好日子，而忽视了对世界的责任。这种对美好生活的狭隘 <u> 看法 </u> 可能会带来 <u> 短期 </u> 利益，但必然导致 <u> 长期的伤害 </u> 和 <u> 痛苦 </u> 。建立在舒适和 <u> 奢华基础 </u> 上的美好生活，最终可能会引发更多的 <u> 痛苦 </u> ，因为我们 <u> 损害 </u> 了自己的 <u> 健康 </u> ，甚至是自己的品格、 <u> 原则 </u> 、 <u> 理想 </u> 和人际关系。"
    },
    {
      "num": "03",
      "en": "What then, is the {secret} of a good life? A good life is a process, not a state of being: a direction, not a destination.We have to earn a good life by first serving others without any {expectation} in return because their {happiness} is the very source of our own happiness.More {importantly} , we {must} know {ourselves} {inside} out.Only when we examine ourselves {deeply} can we discover our abilities and recognize our limitations, and then work accordingly to create a better world.",
      "cn": "那么，美好生活的 <u> 秘诀 </u> 是什么呢？美好的生活是一个过程，而不是一种状态：它是一个方向，而不是一个终点。我们首先必须要不 <u> 求 </u> 回报地为他人服务，以此来赢得美好的生活，因为他人的 <u> 幸福 </u> 正是我们自身幸福的源泉。更 <u> 重要 </u> 的是，我们 <u> 必须彻底 </u> 了解 <u> 自己 </u> 。我们只有 <u> 深刻地 </u> 审视自己，才能发现自己的能力，认识到自身的局限，并据此努力创造一个更美好的世界。"
    },
    {
      "num": "04",
      "en": "The first {requirement} for a good life is having a loving heart.When we do certain right things merely as a {duty} , we find our job so {tiresome} that we'll soon {burn} out.However, when we do that same job out of love, we not only enjoy what we do, but also do it with an {effortless} feeling.",
      "cn": "美好生活的首要 <u> 条件 </u> 是拥有一颗充满爱的心。当我们仅仅把某些正确的事当作 <u> 责任 </u> 去做时，会发现我们的工作是如此 <u> 乏味 </u> ，以至于我们很快就会 <u> 精疲力竭 </u> 。然而，当我们出于爱去做同样的事情时，我们不仅会乐在其中，还会有一种 <u> 毫不费力的 </u> 感觉。"
    },
    {
      "num": "05",
      "en": "However, love {alone} is {insufficient} to lead a good life.Love sometimes {blinds} us to {reality} . {Consequently} , our good {intentions} may not lead to good results.To achieve desired outcomes, those who want to do good to others also need to {equip} themselves with {accurate} world knowledge. {False} knowledge is more {dangerous} than {ignorance} .If love is the {engine} of a {car} , knowledge is the {steering} {wheel} .If the engine lacks power, the car can't move; if the {driver} loses control of the steering, a road {accident} probably occurs.Only with love in our heart and the right knowledge in our mind can we lead a good life.",
      "cn": "不过， <u> 仅有 </u> 爱还 <u> 不足 </u> 以过上美好的生活。爱有时会让我们 <u> 看不清现实 </u> 。 <u> 因此 </u> ，我们的好 <u> 意 </u> 未必能带来好的结果。为了取得理想的结果，那些想与人为善的人还需要 <u> 具备准确的 </u> 世界知识。 <u> 错误的 </u> 知识比 <u> 无知 </u> 更 <u> 危险 </u> 。如果说爱是 <u> 汽车 </u> 的 <u> 发动机 </u> ，那么知识就是 <u> 方向盘 </u> 。如果发动机缺乏动力，汽车就无法行驶；如果 <u> 司机 </u> 失去对方向盘的控制，就可能发生交通 <u> 事故 </u> 。只有心怀爱意、掌握真知，我们才能过上美好的生活。"
    },
    {
      "num": "06",
      "en": "With love and knowledge, we go all out to create a better world by doing good to others.When we see the {impact} of our good work on the world, we give meaning to our life and earn {lasting} {joy} and happiness.",
      "cn": "带着爱和知识，我们全力以赴，与人为善，以此来创造一个更美好的世界。当我们看到自己的善举对世界产生的 <u> 影响 </u> 时，我们便赋予了自己的生命以意义，并收获了 <u> 持久的快乐 </u> 和幸福。 5NoOncib/NjiX02BpMIzP+Fxyt/ox+WDCb+dhfH7KaYaJ4u5RsVmLondVmcHiLum9J1BQErGzJvzqa5GEIz4ZA=="
    }
  ],
